paragraph('The release fit has $f=0.28161$',r'The release fit has $f=0.274245$ and $H_0=68.9389\,\mathrm{km\,s^{-1}\,Mpc^{-1}}$. The five fitted parameters are $(\omega_b,f,\ln(10^{10}A_s),n_s,\tau)$, with the formation ratio fixed at $5.333$; the reference has six parameters. These are local optimized fits, re-evaluated at higher accuracy, with zero massive-neutrino mass and the same simplified low-$\ell$ treatment. The difference $\Delta\chi^2=-0.515$ is a statistical tie at this level of model development; the conditional parameter-count comparison gives $\Delta\mathrm{AIC}=-2.515$. ACT primary-spectrum and lensing checks are reported separately in Section~27. The assembly history and its astrophysical prior, a validated nonlinear response, and a full joint likelihood remain to be determined. The low-density completion of O.3 preserves the fitted cold linear branch.')
